# ------------------------------------------------- QQ 客户端副本（runtime/）
# 完整客户端约 1.1 GB（~1900 个文件，其中 wrapper.node 单个 110 MB），远超声
# 仓库能承受的范围，也不属于本项目源码。
#
# 首次运行时会自动下载锁定版本（src/qsick/runtime_fetch.py），来源是
# http://49.235.134.245/qq_got/QQNT-9.9.33-52230。目录已存在时直接跳过，
# 不会覆盖用户手工放入的版本。可用 QSICK_RUNTIME_URL 指向镜像，
# QSICK_SKIP_RUNTIME_DOWNLOAD=1 关闭自动下载。
runtime/
runtime.download.tar.gz
runtime.staging/

# --------------------------------------------------------- local cache/scratch
.uv-cache/
.env
/tmp*/
# 项目内临时目录：所有临时产物（上传中转、解包暂存、截图、审计输出、探针脚本）
# 都放这里，不再散落到系统 %TEMP%。src/qsick/tempdir.py 是唯一的入口，
# 可以用 QSICK_TEMP_DIR 指到别处（并行测试时每个 worker 各一份）。
/temp/

# pytest tmp dirs when the base temp is the project root
pytest-of-*/
pytest-cache-files-*/
.ptmp*/

# Short-lived pytest --basetemp directories used while verifying a change.
#
# These are created ad hoc (`.w1`, `.v8`, `.pte3` …) and deleted when the run finishes -- but a run that
# is interrupted leaves one behind, and `git add -A` then commits thousands of test artifacts.
#
# gitignore has no `{n,m}` quantifier, so this matches "a dot followed by lowercase letters/digits, as a
# directory at the repo root". `.venv`, `.idea` and `.vscode` are already ignored by their own rules, and
# matching them here again is harmless.
/.[a-z]*/

# Node
node_modules/

# ============================ injected DLLs: binaries ship, sources do not.
#
# The compiled DLLs are part of the distribution -- the project cannot run without them, and a clone
# that is missing them is not usable. What stays private is how they are built: the C++, headers,
# build scripts, offsets and the notes that describe the internals.
#
# This keeps the earlier arrangement for `qsick_payload` (binary only) and applies the same split to
# `qsick_pipe` and the QQNT shim, which previously shipped with full sources.
#
# Ignore the sources first, then re-include the binaries. Order matters: git applies rules in sequence
# and the last matching rule wins, so the negations have to come after the broad patterns.

# --- C++ sources and headers
native/**/*.cpp
native/**/*.cc
native/**/*.c
native/**/*.h
native/**/*.hpp
native/**/*.asm

# --- build inputs and scripts
native/**/*.bat
native/**/*.def
native/**/*.rc
native/**/*.res
native/**/*.sln
native/**/*.vcxproj
native/**/*.props
native/**/*.py

# --- link intermediates and test hosts
native/**/*.obj
native/**/*.lib
native/**/*.exp
native/**/*.pdb
native/**/*.ilk
native/**/*.exe
native/**/__pycache__/

# --- notes that describe the internals, and the per-build offset table
native/qsick-payload/README.md
native/qsick-payload/NATIVE-NOTICE.md
native/qsick-payload/BUILD.txt
native/qsick-payload/offsets.json
native/**/build/

# --- the DLLs themselves stay tracked
!native/**/*.dll

# --- QQNT host shim: same split. Sources private, QQNT.dll shipped.
build/*.cpp
build/*.asm
build/*.def
build/*.bat
!build/QQNT.dll

build/*.pdb
build/*.ilk
build/*.tlog

# ==================================================== local test / probe scripts
#
# The probes and one-off verifiers written while reverse-engineering are scaffolding, not product: they
# encode a question that was worth asking once ("does uploadFile take one argument?") and their value
# expires as soon as the answer is known. They stay on disk and out of the repository.
#
# `tests/` is NOT covered by anything here. That is the project's real suite -- the one `pytest` runs
# and the one that has been catching regressions all along. Excluding it would leave every future change
# unverified, which is the opposite of what these rules are for.
#
# The patterns below are matched against the file name inside tools/, so a genuine utility survives even
# if its name happens to contain one of these words in the middle.
tools/probe_*
tools/*_probe.js
tools/check_*
tools/record_*
tools/inspect_*
tools/fix_*
tools/debug_*
tools/inventory_*
tools/capture*
tools/decode_*
tools/dump_*
tools/download_*
tools/extract_*
tools/test_*
tools/verify_*
tools/watch_*
tools/measure_*
tools/diagnose_*
tools/diag_*
tools/show_*
tools/search_*
tools/serve_for_verify.py
tools/build_purge_list.py
tools/compat_test_fix.py
# Reverse-engineering helpers whose names do not start with one of the prefixes above. Listed
# individually because each was written to answer one question and none is used by the product.
tools/compare_session_lookup.py
tools/export_fake_forward.py
tools/find_forward_params.py
tools/get_session_via_engine.py
tools/install_rspbuffer_hook.py
tools/payload_diag.py
tools/pe_probe.py
tools/remote_exec.py
tools/remote_push.py
tools/inventory_tracked.py

# Anything dropped here by a scratch run rather than by a person.
temp/
scratch/

